    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-5480",
      "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14151255/assets/f1d13a5ffd6de0d3ac42111b14a2fc65d1630839fe3dd64fe4b8d28a7b1bf741.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14151255/assets/af38441c601bf7e3e2c2fdf00104b91bd045deedc8748cecb59bcdc4531ae788.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$",
